00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.840
So here's the problem we all run into.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.840
You spend an hour with an AI, right?

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.400
You're explaining your business, your specific offer,

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.320
maybe what you decided last month, you

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.080
get it to a really great place.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.080
But then the chat ends, and that next

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.200
conversation, it just starts completely from zero.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.400
Now the AI didn't forget on purpose, it simply never

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.800
had anywhere to actually keep what you told it.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.840
Continuum gives it somewhere to keep it.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.680
If you think about how your own memory

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.480
works, scientists generally describe it in two main

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.440
layers Layer one is your working memory.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.600
That's just the handful of things you're holding in your

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.000
mind right now, this very minute while you work.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.560
Then layer two is your long-term memory,

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.560
which actually splits into two halves.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.000
One half is your semantic memory, basically what you know,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.520
your facts, your preferences, decisions you've made over time.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.270
The other half is episodic memory, which is what happened.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:10.150
Those are specific moments you can actually go back to.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:13.510
And underneath both of those is the record itself, meaning

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.390
the notes and files those memories originally came from.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:17.830
I'd like you to hold on to this

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:21.030
picture, because Continuum is built exactly this way.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.510
So how does all this connect to your AI?

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.350
Well, when people say an AI has

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.190
context, they really just mean whatever is

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:28.470
right in front of it right now.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:29.990
That is its working memory.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:31.350
Anything that isn't right there in front

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.030
of it, it simply cannot use.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.790
So the whole game here is context management, deciding exactly

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:39.510
what goes in front of the AI and when, and

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:42.230
keeping everything else somewhere it can be found really fast.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:44.630
That's what a second brain actually is.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:46.870
Continuum does this context management for

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.710
you, right from your own history.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.510
Continuum has these exact same layers.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.790
First, your working memory is essentially your constitution.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:57.030
It's an in depth document all about you,

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.670
and it's written from your own conversations, who

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.990
you are, what you're building, how you work.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.840
What you never want, and how you want help.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.160
Your AI reads all of this at the start of

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.440
every single conversation, completely without you having to ask.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.640
Then, right behind it, your semantic memory holds every

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:16.440
finding that constitution was written from, with each one

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.160
tied directly to the exact words you said.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.880
Next, your episodic memory is every conversation

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.440
you've ever had with ChatGPT or Claude.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.720
It's fully searchable.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.000
So your AI can go back

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.440
and find the exact moment.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:31.880
And underneath it all, your original files never change.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.880
So what does that actually do

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.400
for you, day to day?

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.480
Well, your constitution means your AI

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.880
starts every conversation already knowing you.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.560
And I don't just mean the basics.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.280
When a topic comes up, let's say pricing, it can

